{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#recovery-request",
  "description": "The request for a recovery (avalon_protocol::identity_id::recovery_request_signing_bytes): tag avalon.recovery.request, layout version 1, fields network_id (str), the recovering identity_id (32 raw bytes), request_id (uuid, also the id of the new signing key), the new public key (algorithm byte + 32 raw bytes) and the 32-byte chain hash of the identity.recovery_configured event the request relies on. The holder of the new key signs it (signingKeySeedHex stands in for the new key); it is the signature of the identity.recovery_requested marker. The layout is the structured signing-bytes encoding (avalon_protocol::signing_bytes): the ASCII domain tag with no length, a u16 big-endian layout version (1) and a u32 big-endian rules version (1), then the fields in the order listed, then the extensions region (count u16 = 0: 00 00). str is a u32 big-endian byte length and the UTF-8 bytes; uuid is its 16 raw bytes; identity ids are 32 raw bytes; a public key is the algorithm byte 01 (Ed25519) then its 32 raw bytes; seq is a u64 big-endian, followed by the hash algorithm byte 01 (SHA-256) and prev_hash, one byte (0 = no previous event, 1 = a 32-byte event hash follows). The signature is Ed25519 by the signer key over the bytes, verified strictly. replayVectors offer a signature made for one input with another input's bytes; it must not verify. There is no legacy layout.",
  "generation": "Generated by scripts/gen-identity-key-event-vectors.py, an encoder that shares no code with the Rust one (cryptography Ed25519, hashlib). signingKeySeedHex is the Ed25519 seed of the signer; Ed25519 signatures are deterministic.",
